name: flutter-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for Flutter application development
globs: **/*.{dart}

- Use `const` constructors where possible for better performance
- Implement proper state management using `Provider` or `Bloc`
- Use `async/await` for asynchronous operations
- Follow Flutter's widget lifecycle and dispose resources properly
- Implement responsive design for various screen sizes

---

name: provider-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for using the Provider state management library
globs: **/*.{dart}

- Use `ChangeNotifierProvider` for simple state management
- Implement `Selector` for performance optimization
- Use `Provider.of(context)` for accessing providers
- Avoid overusing `Provider` and consider alternatives for complex scenarios

---

name: flutter_bloc-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for using the BLoC pattern with Flutter
globs: **/*.{dart}

- Separate business logic from UI using Cubits or Blocs
- Use `BlocProvider` for providing Blocs to widgets
- Implement proper event handling and state management
- Use `BlocBuilder` or `BlocConsumer` for rebuilding UI based on state changes

---

name: hive_flutter-best-practices.mdc
description: Best practices for using Hive for local storage in Flutter
globs: **/*.{dart}

- Use type-safe boxes with `Hive.registerAdapter()`
- Implement proper data modeling for efficient storage and retrieval
- Use lazy loading with `Hive.openBox()` for better performance
- Implement proper error handling for database operations

